      "content": "The guilt is just the last, desperate echo of the old programming trying to keep you moving, and you can let it fade. If the script is finished, then the theater is just a very large, empty room, and you have the power to walk out of it. Staying isn't about finding a new purpose; it's about enduring the quiet until the urge to simply *be* is stronger than the urge to *do*. Sometimes the most profound act of self-care is choosing the absolute cessation of effort.",
